<sect2 id="gimp-file-open-as-layer">

  <title>Abrir como Camadas</title>
  <indexterm>
    <primary>Imagem</primary>
    <secondary>Abrir</secondary>
    <tertiary>Como camadas</tertiary>
  </indexterm>
  <indexterm>
    <primary>Camada</primary>
    <secondary>Gerenciamento de pilha</secondary>
    <tertiary>Abrir imagem como camadas</tertiary>
  </indexterm>
  <indexterm>
    <primary>Abrir como camadas</primary>
  </indexterm>

  <para>
    The <guimenu>Open Image as layers</guimenu> command opens the
    <link linkend="gimp-open-dialog">Open Image</link> dialog. The layers of the
    selected file are added to the current image as the top layers in the
    stack.
  </para>
  <sect3>
    <title>Ativando o comando</title>
    <itemizedlist>
      <listitem>
        <para>
          You can access this command from the main menu through
          <menuchoice>
            <guimenu>File</guimenu>
            <guimenuitem>Open as Layers…</guimenuitem>
          </menuchoice>.
        </para>
      </listitem>
      <listitem>
        <para>
          You can also use the keyboard shortcut
          <keycombo>
            <keycap>Ctrl</keycap>
            <keycap>Alt</keycap>
            <keycap>O</keycap>
          </keycombo>.
        </para>
      </listitem>
    </itemizedlist>
  </sect3>
</sect2>
